    "bitcoin_integration": "Crypto is legal and actively regulated. The Bahamas pioneered a bespoke digital-asset regime: the Digital Assets and Registered Exchanges (DARE) Act 2020, superseded by the DARE Act 2024 (in force 31 July 2024), administered by the Securities Commission of The Bahamas. It licenses/registers digital-asset exchanges, custodians and token issuers and covers stablecoins and staking disclosure. The central bank has also piloted a CBDC (the 'Sand Dollar'). Bitcoin and other digital assets are therefore lawful subject to SCB registration/licensing."
